{
 "_doc": "Shared samples for create.board.scrub_paths' generic rules (QUA-2946, QUA-2950, QUA-2953): each 'in' scrubbed (with a runs dir and home that occur in none of them) must equal 'out', and scrubbing 'out' again must leave it unchanged. Any port of the rule must pass the same list. User names are synthetic. A path, or an ls -l line, may also start right after a JSON-escaped newline, carriage return or tab (backslash + n, r or t). An ls -l line's owner column becomes <user>; its group stays.",
